1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:07,302
Before you can carve a cathedral out of a mountain, you must perform an act of sheer violence against the earth itself.

2
00:00:07,252 --> 00:00:14,270
In the winter of 756 CE, ten thousand stonecutters climbed the Charanandri ridge.

3
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:17,395
They did not begin by carving gods.

4
00:00:17,395 --> 00:00:22,695
They began by cutting three colossal trenches straight down into the crust of India.

5
00:00:22,695 --> 00:00:26,093
Two side trenches eighty-four meters long.

6
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:29,895
One back scarp trench forty-seven meters wide.

7
00:00:29,895 --> 00:00:35,039
Together, they formed a massive U-shaped chasm thirty-three meters deep.

8
00:00:35,039 --> 00:00:40,833
Inside that chasm sat four hundred thousand tons of suffocating volcanic basalt.

9
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:45,859
To free the temple, every single pebble had to be excavated by hand.

10
00:00:45,859 --> 00:00:48,385
And their enemy was not time.

11
00:00:48,385 --> 00:00:52,057
Their enemy was the hardest rock on planet Earth.

